{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"steep-tired-whimbrel","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n`gate_enabled` (src/rebar/_commands/gates.py:79-87) returns a BARE BOOL that is `False` for TWO\nmaterially different states:\n\n  * the gate is genuinely turned off (a deliberate policy choice), and\n  * the gate's configuration could not be READ (a fault).\n\nWorse, the unreadable case **fails OPEN**. An unreadable or malformed config therefore silently\nDISABLES the completion-verification gate, and every downstream reader — including\n`_completion_precheck` — sees a state indistinguishable from an operator having turned the gate off\non purpose. A fault is laundered into a policy choice, and the gate stops protecting anything\nwithout anyone being told.\n\nThis is a latent defect with standalone value: it is worth fixing whether or not any dependent work\nis ever built.\n\n## Approach\nReturn a TRI-STATE (gate on / gate off / gate config unreadable) instead of a bool, and fail CLOSED\non unreadable rather than open. Fix it at the SOURCE in `gate_enabled` rather than recomputing the\ndistinction at each call site — a second config read in a second place is a copy that will drift out\nof sync with the first.\n\nUpdate all callers to handle the third state explicitly rather than defaulting it into either\nexisting branch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `gate_enabled` returns a three-valued result distinguishing enabled / disabled /\n      config-unreadable; no caller can conflate the latter two.\n- [ ] An unreadable or malformed gate config FAILS CLOSED (the gate is treated as active), and the\n      condition is surfaced rather than swallowed.\n- [ ] A held-out test seeds an unreadable config and asserts the gate does NOT silently disable —\n      demonstrated RED before the fix, not merely green after.\n- [ ] Every existing `gate_enabled` caller is updated to handle the third state explicitly; a grep\n      for call sites shows none relying on bool truthiness.\n- [ ] Existing gate on/off behaviour is unchanged for readable configs (existing tests pass unmodified).\n\n## Provenance\nSplit out per operator decision 2026-08-19 from `mechanical-coherent-wolverine` (23b2-1a94), where\nthis surfaced as plan-review R3's first blocking finding: 'gate_enabled must distinguish gate-off\nfrom config-unreadable, or the expectation must be computed somewhere that can see the difference.\nIts current fail-open bool is the blocker.' It is filed separately because the defect stands on its\nown, and because wolverine cannot author its `gate_unreadable` acceptance criteria until this\ntri-state's shape is settled.\n\nCoordinate with RP-06 (`uneducated-habitual-primate`, 'Unified effective-policy discovery for review\ngates'): RP-06's effective-policy snapshot should CONSUME this tri-state, not produce its own. This\nwas deliberately NOT folded into RP-06 so that a small, independently-landable fix is not coupled to\na large program's schedule.","id":"f5c4-b2d1-4503-4bfe","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"gate_enabled fails OPEN and collapses gate-off with config-unreadable"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787175607648248001,"uuid":"b85e143d-55d1-40ff-8c76-f1681a5e7f59"}